 "title": "50 Ω LTCC ceramic low-pass filter, DC to 1000 MHz",
 "source": {
  "revision": "REV. R, ECO-023234",
  "pages": 3
 },
 "summary": "A seven-section low-pass filter for 50 Ω lines, built in low-temperature co-fired ceramic and housed in the four-terminal FV1206 surface-mount case. It passes DC to 1000 MHz with at most 1.0 dB loss, is 3 dB down near 1300 MHz, and typically rejects 30 dB from 1900 to 5000 MHz. It takes up to 10 W of RF input at 25 °C. Uses named for it are harmonic rejection, VHF and UHF transmitters and receivers, and lab work.",
