 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Seven filter sections in LTCC ceramic, a ladder of series inductors with shunt capacitors to ground between RF IN and RF OUT. It is temperature stable and covered by U.S. patent 6,943,646."
  },
  {
   "topic": "DC on the ports",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The filter is not to carry DC: with a DC voltage on the input or the output, put a coupling capacitor in series with that port. A version with the suffix D passes DC from input to output and holds more than 100 MOhm of isolation to ground."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "10 W of RF input is allowed in the passband at 25°C ambient. The limit drops linearly with ambient temperature, reaching 3.5 W at 100°C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Demo board layout",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Test board TB-270 follows layout PL-137. Its RF lines are coplanar waveguide, 0.038 in wide with a 0.013 in gap each side, on Rogers RO4350B 0.020 in ± 0.0015 in thick with 1/2 oz copper per side; the bottom side is a continuous ground plane. The top ground carries eight 0.015 in plated through holes. With a different laminate the trace width and gap may need changing. Layout dimensions: 0.098 in, 0.072 in typ, 0.021 in typ, 0.028 in typ, 0.024 in typ, 0.019 in (2 places). Board copper outside the land pattern is under solder mask (SMOBC); the land pattern has no mask."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Land pattern",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The suggested footprint has a pad at each end for RF IN and RF OUT and, between them, two ground pads, each with a plated through hole of diameter N to the ground plane. Its dimensions hold to within ±0.002 in."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The body carries the code MU. Letters and numbers can appear on the top, and the shape of the ground terminations varies."
  }
 ],
